### Tests for the Identity and Administration API (Daniel)
### Click "Send Request" above each test. The comment says what should come back.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3003
# Cloudflare's test ticket. With the test secret key it always passes.
@ticket = XXXX.DUMMY.TOKEN.XXXX

### T1. Health check  -> 200 "status": "ok"
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health

### T2. Sign up WITHOUT a Turnstile ticket  -> 403 BOT_CHECK_FAILED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Test Student", "email": "daniel.test.student@example.com", "password": "Student123", "role": "student" }

### T3. Sign up a student (correct)  -> 201, accountStatus "pending"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
X-Turnstile-Token: {{ticket}}

{ "name": "Test Student", "email": "daniel.test.student@example.com", "password": "Student123", "role": "student" }

### T4. Same email again  -> 409 EMAIL_ALREADY_REGISTERED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
X-Turnstile-Token: {{ticket}}

{ "name": "Copy Cat", "email": "daniel.test.student@example.com", "password": "Student123", "role": "student" }

### T5. Try to sign up as admin  -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
X-Turnstile-Token: {{ticket}}

{ "name": "Sneaky", "email": "daniel.test.sneaky@example.com", "password": "Sneaky123", "role": "admin" }

### T6. Weak password  -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
X-Turnstile-Token: {{ticket}}

{ "name": "Weak", "email": "daniel.test.weak@example.com", "password": "123", "role": "student" }

### T7. Log in while still pending  -> 403 ACCOUNT_PENDING
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-Turnstile-Token: {{ticket}}

{ "email": "daniel.test.student@example.com", "password": "Student123" }

### T8. Log in with the WRONG password  -> 401 "Email or password is incorrect."
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-Turnstile-Token: {{ticket}}

{ "email": "daniel.test.student@example.com", "password": "Wrong12345" }

### T9. Log in with an email that doesn't exist  -> 401, SAME message as T8
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-Turnstile-Token: {{ticket}}

{ "email": "nobody@example.com", "password": "Whatever123" }